<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Riau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Riau is a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> on the east coast of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, with its capital at Pekanbaru. Crossed by the Siak, Kampar, Indragiri and Rokan rivers, it was home to Malay sultanates such as Siak and Indragiri. Today it is a major producer of oil and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palm-oil">palm oil</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/riau.jpg" alt="Riau" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Riau_in_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
